92186045417 true] [17592186425828 1074 "We have $\\frac{3}{4}$ on the left and $\\frac{3}{8}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/50/5091a3f982e94ea27aea26a45b47bf768980dbc802f52905d0ecfc78e111f3ef.png)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{8}\n$$" 13194139534562 17592186045417 true] [17592186425829 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425825 13194139534562 17592186045417 true] [17592186425829 1069 "q-60226" 13194139534562 17592186045417 true] [17592186425829 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534562 17592186045417 true] [17592186425829 1071 "![](images/0e/0e8213704b9b6ba8e507ec59a09d5e6fe1450e21fa3e1f26eca15876a5807fdc.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\frac{2}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{3}.$" 13194139534562 17592186045417 true] [17592186425829 1072 #uuid "8fb4c868-ce54-5c7d-ab79-c96f1e73ab38" 13194139534562 17592186045417 true] [17592186425829 1074 "Since we need to multiply by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/37/37d524644c009517608455822101750eb532cc8858fee1b96516d30e3fa1fe15.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{2}{12}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2}{12}.\n$$" 13194139534562 17592186045417 true] [17592186425830 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425822 13194139534562 17592186045417 true] [17592186425830 1069 "q-137179" 13194139534562 17592186045417 true] [17592186425830 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534562 17592186045417 true] [17592186425830 1071 "![](images/26/26520b2b179e8d2bac0b20552d670d8503d734d22bafacb741edb2efce649f4d.png)\n\nWhat multiplication problem is represented by the model above?" 13194139534562 17592186045417 true] [17592186425830 1072 #uuid "952e22b6-fb4f-5a48-8331-618041da94da" 13194139534562 17592186045417 true] [17592186425830 1074 "We have $\\frac{2}{5}$ on the left and $\\frac{2}{10}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/40/40183e8f591be9be4dbffc83e45958d184674a4bb